gambatte-pico patch to upstream gambatte (libgambatte/include/gambatte.h, libgambatte/src/
gambatte.cpp, gambatte-memory.cpp, gambatte-memory.h, initstate.cpp, savestate.h, statesaver.cpp,
mem/cartridge.cpp, mem/cartridge.h, mem/cartridge_libretro.cpp, and the new mem/mbc7.cpp and
mem/mbc7.h), GPL-2.0 like the files it changes. Copyright (c) 2026 TheGammaSqueeze. Applied by
build.sh to a copy in out/src.

MBC7 cartridges (Kirby Tilt 'n' Tumble, Command Master) load instead of being refused. The
mapper banks ROM like MBC5 with a seven bit number; A000-AFFF is a window onto the cartridge's
two axis accelerometer and its 93LC56 serial EEPROM, reached through the same path as an RTC's
registers. The EEPROM is the battery save (256 bytes), and the chip goes into save states under
two new labels, which older states simply lack. GB::setAccelerometer gives the core the sensor's
reading; GB::hasAccelerometer tells the frontend when to feed it.

